From 9be325ca59b2298123506561bd7f82e849504b56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:00:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] The separation of the 3D window follows the person's depth
 limits from the desktop

render.stereo_eye_angle is zero by default and then the two cameras' separation is the largest one under which the nearest
and farthest point of the scene stay inside the sunk and popped limits Stereo KWin gives the window (libstereo-declare 1.10,
_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_DEPTH_LIMITS), and follows a change of them. With no limits the eyes are the same picture and the program
says so, in the ten languages. window::pollStereoDepth reports the state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
